603	    /**
604	     * Resolves the effective registration date for a create, rolled onto a business day. The
605	     * supplied date is used when present, otherwise the server's current date; either way the result
606	     * is rolled forward to the next Monday when it falls on a Saturday or Sunday (see
607	     * {@link BusinessDayAdjuster#toBusinessDay}). Every value derived from the registration date - the
608	     * stored {@code registrationDate}, the membership number's year segment and the daily
609	     * create-limit's per-day count - is judged on this adjusted date.
610	     *
611	     * @param suppliedRegistrationDate the registration date from the request, or {@code null} to
612	     *                                 default to the server's current date
613	     * @return the effective registration date, guaranteed to fall on a business day
614	     */
615	    /**
616	     * Rejects a create whose supplied {@code registrationDate} lies after the server's current date.
617	     * The raw submitted value is compared against {@link LocalDate#now()} before any business-day
618	     * adjustment; a future date cannot describe a registration that has already happened, so it is
619	     * reported as a {@code 400 Bad Request}. A {@code null} registration date (defaulted to the
620	     * server's current date) and any date on or before today are accepted.
621	     *
622	     * @param suppliedRegistrationDate the registration date from the request, or {@code null} when
623	     *                                 omitted
624	     * @throws InvalidOwnerFieldsException if the supplied date is later than the server's current date
625	     */
626	    private void rejectFutureRegistrationDate(LocalDate suppliedRegistrationDate) {
627	        if (suppliedRegistrationDate != null && suppliedRegistrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
628	            throw new InvalidOwnerFieldsException(List.of("registrationDate"));
629	        }
630	    }
